Official doc:  AWS EKS Cluster Upgrade Guide￼

Here’s the practical DevOps interview + real-world summary:

⸻

EKS Upgrade Flow

1. Check current cluster version

kubectl version
kubectl get nodes

Control plane and worker nodes should ideally be on the same version before upgrade.  

⸻

Important Rules

You can upgrade only ONE minor version at a time

Example:

1.28 → 1.29 → 1.30

NOT:

1.28 → 1.30

⸻

Recommended Upgrade Order

Step 1: Backup & Validate

Check:

* Deprecated APIs
* Cluster health
* Add-ons compatibility
* Node versions
* IP availability in subnets

AWS recommends using Upgrade Insights before upgrading.  

⸻

Step 2: Upgrade Control Plane

Using AWS CLI:

aws eks update-cluster-version \
  --name my-cluster \
  --kubernetes-version 1.30 \
  --region ap-south-1

Monitor:

aws eks describe-update \
  --name my-cluster \
  --update-id <id> \
  --region ap-south-1

⸻

Step 3: Upgrade Node Groups

Managed node groups:

eksctl upgrade nodegroup \
  --cluster my-cluster \
  --name my-nodegroup

Or update via console.

AWS replaces old EC2 worker nodes gradually using rolling updates.  

⸻

Step 4: Upgrade Add-ons

Very important in interviews.

Update:

* VPC CNI
* CoreDNS
* kube-proxy
* EBS CSI Driver
* Cluster Autoscaler

Many real-world failures happen because add-ons are outdated.  

⸻

Step 5: Validate

kubectl get nodes
kubectl get pods -A

Check:

* Pods healthy
* Ingress working
* DNS working
* Autoscaler working
* Monitoring agents healthy

⸻

Common Real-World Problems

Problem	Cause
NodeCreationFailure	Networking or add-on mismatch
Nodes not joining	Security groups / IAM / subnet issues
Ingress breaks	API deprecations
Upgrade stuck	Deprecated APIs
Pods crash	Old manifests

Examples from engineers on Reddit show failures mostly due to:

* outdated CoreDNS/VPC-CNI
* node networking
* unsupported APIs  

⸻

Best Practice Used in Companies

Blue-Green Upgrade

Instead of in-place upgrade:

1. Create new EKS cluster
2. Deploy apps
3. Test
4. Switch traffic
5. Destroy old cluster

Safer for production.  

⸻

Important Interview Points

Why EKS upgrades matter?

* Security patches
* Kubernetes support lifecycle
* New features
* Avoid deprecated APIs

⸻

Commands Interviewers Expect

eksctl

eksctl upgrade cluster \
  --name my-cluster \
  --version 1.30 \
  --approve

⸻

Golden Rule

Always upgrade in this order:

Control Plane
→ Node Groups
→ Add-ons
→ Applications
→ kubectl clients